.TH PSMatrixTranspose 3 2023-12-07 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSMatrixTranspose

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSMatrixTranspose\fR(\fIPSMatrix matrix\fR, \fIint rebuild\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Transpose \fImatrix\fR by swapping its first dimension with its last dimension. For example, a matrix with a shape of 2,3 will be transposed to a matrix with shape of 3,2.
.br
The function won't modify \fImatrix\fR but it will create a new matrix that is the transposed version of \fImatrix\fR.
.br
The trasponsed matrix is cached in the private data of \fImatrix\fR so that subsequent calls of this function with the same \fImatrix\fR and with \fIrebuild\fR argument set to zero will directly return the cached transposed matrix without recomputing the transposition.
.br
The \fIrebuild\fR argument can be used to invalidate the cached transposed matrix forcing the function to rebuild it.
.br
If \fImatrix\fR already is the cached transposed matrix of another matrix, the function will directly return the source matrix of \fImatrix\fR.
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.
.br

.br
\fBWARN\fR:  The cached transposed matrix is automatically freed by freeing its owner (\fImatrix\fR) with \fIPSMatrixFree\fR, so it should not be freed directly. In order to free and reset the transposed cached matrix, the function \fIPSMatrixResetTransposed\fR should be called on \fImatrix\fR.
.br

.br
\fBWARN\fR:  most of the functions who alter the original matrix (\fImatrix\fR) will also invalidate the cached transposed matrix if any. However, manually changing matrix's values would lead to inconsistency between the matrix and its transposed version so the transposed matrix should be invalidated with \fIPSMatrixResetTransposed\fR or rebuilt by calling \fIPSMatrixTranspose\fR with \fIrebuild\fR argument set to true.
.br

.SH RETURN VALUES
The transposed matrix or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fImatrix\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] Memory canmot be allocated.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
PSMatrixFree(3), PSMatrixResetTransposed(3), PSMatrixSwapAxes(3)
